1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:24,937
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,667
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:37,497
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:40,897
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you.

7
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:43,557
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, and so elusive.

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,717
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:51,857
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,697
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,597
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:08,897
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:11,940
Believe in wonderland.

17
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:21,117
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,917
We live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,537
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:36,637
We don't want to live ordinary lives.

24
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:39,777
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:42,760
We live in wonderland.

26
00:02:01,980 --> 00:02:03,820
Hey, quit slacking on! Ouch!

27
00:02:04,220 --> 00:02:06,917
Hey, chore boys, wash the windows
when you're finished here.

28
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:07,830
Sir!

29
00:02:08,040 --> 00:02:16,469
One, two, three, four.

30
00:02:16,552 --> 00:02:17,382
One, two.

31
00:02:17,465 --> 00:02:18,840
Uh, I can't stand this.

32
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:23,275
Kobe can be the model chore boy if
he wants, but why do I have to do it?

33
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:26,510
Damn it,

34
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:31,188
if it weren't for that stupid Straw Hat
guy, none of this would have happened?

35
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:33,220
It's all his fault,

36
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:35,117
it's because of that straw
hat guy that I'm here

37
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:38,259
doing stupid chores instead
of living the good life!

38
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:39,230
Hey, Hellnipo?

39
00:02:39,313 --> 00:02:40,157
What do you want?

40
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:41,577
Why are you touching me like that?

41
00:02:41,660 --> 00:02:43,837
You shouldn't blame
everything on Luffy like that,

42
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:46,077
it isn't his fault, he was
just doing the right thing.

43
00:02:46,160 --> 00:02:49,457
For a long time you could use your
father's power to get through life.

44
00:02:49,540 --> 00:02:51,060
Things are different now.

45
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:55,197
We've got to work long and hard on
our own to accomplish our dreams.

46
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:56,120
Oh, please.

47
00:02:56,720 --> 00:02:57,960
You know my dream?

48
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:01,277
Someday I'm going to be a
great officer in the Marines.

49
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:03,700
I'll chase bad guys and defend justice.

50
00:03:07,220 --> 00:03:08,700
How stupid can you be?

51
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:11,797
A wimp like you becoming a
Marine officer like my dad?

52
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:13,357
No way that will ever happen.

53
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:14,616
I know that it will.

54
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:17,697
Thanks to Luffy, I know that
I can do anything that I want.

55
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:18,610
That's right!

56
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:20,597
I'm gonna be King of the Pirates!

57
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:24,680
I decided that long ago, and if I
die fighting for it, it's alright!

58
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:27,717
So I decided to be like
Luffy and do anything,

59
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:30,388
even risk my life, to
achieve my final goal!

60
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:34,194
Well, now we can work hard
and reach our goals together!

61
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:35,230
Get it!

62
00:03:35,313 --> 00:03:36,557
You think I'm going to listen to this?

63
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:39,377
What the heck makes you think
you can tell me what I should do?

64
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:42,957
And what could you have possibly learned
from that pathetic excuse for a pirate?

65
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:44,877
Don't talk about Luffy like that!

66
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:47,197
I haven't done anything
but try to help you out!

67
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:49,515
I don't remember asking for your help!

68
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:52,717
Help that fool, will you please?

69
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:53,976
Stop acting foolish!

70
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:55,917
Oh, please, you're calling me a fool?

71
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:56,830
Take that!

72
00:03:56,980 --> 00:03:58,137
Would you stop coming?

73
00:03:58,220 --> 00:03:59,257
I've got some more!

74
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:00,575
What's going on here?

75
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:20,760
We're sorry, sir!

76
00:04:24,380 --> 00:04:25,210
Really?

77
00:04:25,293 --> 00:04:27,377
That explosion earlier was from you guys?

78
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:30,177
They didn't kick you out of
the Marines, did they, Kobe?

79
00:04:30,260 --> 00:04:31,319
Thank you, ma 'am.

80
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:34,266
No, they actually allowed
us to stay enlisted.

81
00:04:35,340 --> 00:04:38,634
Yeah, but we had to agree to
work for free for 50 years.

82
00:04:39,260 --> 00:04:42,201
Getting kicked out would
have been so much better.

83
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:44,450
Attention!

84
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:49,816
I will now inform you about
the nature of our mission.

85
00:04:52,660 --> 00:04:53,880
What do you want?

86
00:04:56,020 --> 00:04:57,340
It's my dad!

87
00:04:58,220 --> 00:05:02,297
Captain Morgan is being sent to Marine
Headquarters to face a court-martial for

88
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:04,937
the crimes of military
exploitation and the

89
00:05:05,020 --> 00:05:07,377
cruel and unusual treatment of civilians.

90
00:05:07,460 --> 00:05:11,380
Our mission is to transfer the
prisoner to Vice Admiral Garden.

91
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:13,540
Reckless lowlife bums!

92
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:16,252
You have no right to defy my superiority!

93
00:05:16,380 --> 00:05:18,439
I am Marine Captain Axe Han Morgan!

94
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:34,134
So I guess it's really going to happen.

95
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:38,976
I mean, I know that he deserves to
get court-martialed and all of that.

96
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:41,960
I get it, given the stuff that he did.

97
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:47,240
But honestly, even after all
that, I still respected him.

98
00:05:56,500 --> 00:05:57,330
Damn it!

99
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:00,130
Why?

100
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:06,320
Kobe, do you think that
they're going to execute him?

101
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:07,960
I don't know.

102
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:14,113
I guess I should probably be ready for
something like that to happen, huh?

103
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:15,820
But he's my dad.

104
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:22,830
Oh, no.

105
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:24,870
Marines!

106
00:06:25,180 --> 00:06:26,520
All hands on deck!

107
00:06:27,380 --> 00:06:28,360
Fall in!

108
00:06:32,380 --> 00:06:34,020
It's Vice Admiral Gar...

109
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:43,960
So that's Marine Vice Admiral
Garp, the man they call the Fist.

110
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:48,282
He's a great hero of the seas who
travels all over the Grand Line.

111
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:58,357
Vice Admiral Garp, thank
you for coming all this way.

112
00:06:58,440 --> 00:07:01,264
We are pleased to deliver
Captain Morgan to you.

113
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:14,177
I heard you.

114
00:07:14,260 --> 00:07:17,417
I'm a bit tired because I've
been up for five days now.

115
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:19,577
You are indeed a dedicated marine, sir.

116
00:07:19,660 --> 00:07:23,497
No, I've been trying to set a record for
the most donuts eaten in a single sitting.

117
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:24,410
Sir?

118
00:07:24,493 --> 00:07:27,697
The sugar kept me going at first,
but I've been at it for a while now,

119
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:31,015
and I guess the lack of sleep
is starting to get to me.

120
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:34,760
Old man, cut the sleeping act already

121
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:44,560
No one move!

122
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:52,285
If anyone moves a muscle, I'll hack this
chore boy up And feed him to the sharks!

123
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:55,300
But, Daddy, why are you doing this?

124
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:56,617
Sir, please stop this!

125
00:07:56,700 --> 00:07:57,797
Remember who is your son?

126
00:07:57,880 --> 00:07:59,697
How can you do something like that to him?

127
00:07:59,780 --> 00:08:00,610
My son?

128
00:08:00,693 --> 00:08:02,189
What do I need with a son?

129
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:04,120
What I want now is freedom.

130
00:08:04,420 --> 00:08:06,100
I don't care about his life.

131
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:09,182
I'll cut him into a thousand
pieces if I have to.

132
00:08:09,940 --> 00:08:10,780
But... Daddy!

133
00:08:13,540 --> 00:08:14,480
Help me!

134
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:16,240
Somebody help me, please!

135
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:18,071
Good riddance, you fools!

136
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:20,680
Ready the cannon.

137
00:08:21,580 --> 00:08:23,440
Load the cannon! Take game!

138
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:25,700
Target, 16 degrees starboard.

139
00:08:25,980 --> 00:08:28,780
Distance, 8263. Now, ready?

140
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:30,610
No!

141
00:08:30,693 --> 00:08:31,559
Please, just wait!

142
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:37,820
I'm begging you not to shoot! Please stop!

143
00:08:38,380 --> 00:08:41,540
He has a hostage on that boat! Move it!

144
00:08:41,940 --> 00:08:42,960
I won't!

145
00:08:44,220 --> 00:08:46,120
In that case, you're dead.

146
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:51,937
Maybe so, but at least I won't be
guilty of abandoning my friends!

147
00:08:52,020 --> 00:08:53,257
Please, I can fix this!

148
00:08:53,340 --> 00:08:54,928
I'll capture Morgan myself!

149
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:09,040
Come back! You idiot!

150
00:09:09,180 --> 00:09:11,497
You'll never be able to
capture him by yourself!

151
00:09:11,580 --> 00:09:12,780
Let's let him try.

152
00:09:13,460 --> 00:09:16,800
He's either brave and dumb, or just dumb.

153
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:20,580
What do we do?

154
00:09:28,220 --> 00:09:29,808
All right, I'm awake again.

155
00:09:29,920 --> 00:09:31,277
Now, what's all this noise about?

156
00:09:31,360 --> 00:09:32,757
Vice Admiral Garp, you're alive.

157
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:34,737
I was certain that monster had killed you.

158
00:09:34,820 --> 00:09:35,650
What?

159
00:09:35,733 --> 00:09:37,144
One of the men has been killed?

160
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:39,977
I can't believe I slept
through something like that.

161
00:09:40,060 --> 00:09:40,980
Who was it?

162
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:47,180
Oh, right.

163
00:09:51,460 --> 00:09:52,780
Free at last!

164
00:09:53,060 --> 00:09:54,080
Just you watch.

165
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:57,097
The world will be kneeling
at my feet again in no time.

166
00:09:57,180 --> 00:09:58,620
I will rule the seas.

167
00:09:58,980 --> 00:10:00,737
The world will quake in terror.

168
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:02,938
Now set our course to the west, boy.

169
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:04,557
What are you doing?

170
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:05,737
I said set our course.

171
00:10:05,820 --> 00:10:06,650
No!

172
00:10:06,780 --> 00:10:07,610
Huh?

173
00:10:07,693 --> 00:10:09,498
I won't have any part in your plans.

174
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:12,417
Kuma put everything on the
line trying to save me.

175
00:10:12,500 --> 00:10:16,057
He even risked getting kicked out of the
Marines to help me, and they're his dream.

176
00:10:16,140 --> 00:10:19,417
He fights for what he believes in
no matter what, and so could I.

177
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:21,380
Dad, I'm going to capture you.

178
00:10:21,520 --> 00:10:23,344
You might as well just give up.

179
00:10:25,140 --> 00:10:26,817
What do you think you're doing, brat?

180
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:29,537
Are you too stupid to know
what you're up against, huh?

181
00:10:29,620 --> 00:10:33,091
What can a useless piece of
scum like you hope to do to me?

182
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:34,910
Damn it.

183
00:10:35,020 --> 00:10:37,737
It's time you learned your
place, you pathetic insect.

184
00:10:37,820 --> 00:10:39,797
No, I'm not listening to you anymore.

185
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:43,821
From now on, I'm the one who's
going to decide how to live my life.

186
00:10:43,980 --> 00:10:45,417
Stop being such an idiot.

187
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:47,537
What could someone like you possibly do?

188
00:10:47,620 --> 00:10:49,267
He can do whatever he wants.

189
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:52,630
You came!

190
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:54,271
Stop right there, Morgan!

191
00:11:01,620 --> 00:11:03,620
You two are absolutely pathetic.

192
00:11:03,880 --> 00:11:07,617
How can a couple of pitiful insects like
you expect to capture someone like me?

193
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:11,117
If you even think about getting
in my way, I'll kill you both!

194
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:12,597
Thank you for coming to save me.

195
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:14,297
I'm sorry it turned out like this.

196
00:11:14,380 --> 00:11:15,400
I'm glad I came.

197
00:11:16,180 --> 00:11:17,827
Aren't we friends after all?

198
00:11:18,360 --> 00:11:19,440
Oh, um, Koby.

199
00:11:24,940 --> 00:11:28,277
You little pests aren't worth the
time it would take to kill you.

200
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:30,595
I'd better never see your faces again.

201
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:32,830
Morgan!

202
00:11:32,913 --> 00:11:35,362
I may have let you sail
away from me alive today,

203
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:38,955
but someday I'm going to
catch you, I promise you that!

204
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:39,922
Do you hear me?

205
00:11:40,060 --> 00:11:42,001
Someday I'm going to capture you!

206
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:43,320
Just you, wait!

207
00:11:47,660 --> 00:11:50,013
Please forgive my poor supervision, sir.

208
00:11:50,200 --> 00:11:52,777
Allowing the prisoner to
escape was inexcusable.

209
00:11:52,860 --> 00:11:54,600
We're very sorry to you, sir!

210
00:11:54,940 --> 00:11:58,822
After today, these two will be
kicked out of the Marines for good.

211
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:02,660
The two of you are truly lost causes.

212
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:04,897
I don't know anyone who
would take you in now.

213
00:12:04,980 --> 00:12:07,980
But turning you loose would
only burden the public.

214
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:12,265
I have no choice but to take you
with me to Marine headquarters.

215
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:13,678
What, Vice Admiral?

216
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:17,017
Sir, you're actually going to take these
two chore boys with you to headquarters?

217
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:18,159
Is that a problem?

218
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:19,200
Of course not.

219
00:12:19,420 --> 00:12:20,655
No problem here, sir.

220
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:22,997
And do you two have a problem?

221
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:25,897
If you want to run away,
this is your last chance.

222
00:12:25,980 --> 00:12:28,921
Not that I'd allow you to
get very far, of course.

223
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:32,358
Well now, this certainly
has been an interesting day.

224
00:12:49,540 --> 00:12:50,370
What?

225
00:12:50,940 --> 00:12:52,116
Marine headquarters?

226
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:53,450
Yeah.

227
00:12:53,540 --> 00:12:56,658
Vice Admiral Garp can be
very unpredictable at times.

228
00:12:57,680 --> 00:13:00,237
He's pretty high up on the
food chain though, right?

229
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:01,760
Yes, very high up.

230
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:07,021
Then those two must have been very promising
to have caught his attention like that.

231
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:13,900
Stupid, stupid, stupid, stupid, stupid!

232
00:13:14,660 --> 00:13:17,960
Why did you let them go
without saying goodbye, stupid?

233
00:13:19,460 --> 00:13:22,040
I still wanted to play
with them some more.

234
00:13:23,660 --> 00:13:25,900
And I wanted to talk to them more.

235
00:13:26,220 --> 00:13:28,220
I was even learning how to cook.

236
00:13:28,860 --> 00:13:34,000
I wanted to make them a yummy lunch next
time they came over, but now I can't.

237
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:38,700
I didn't even get to say
goodbye before they left.

238
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:43,380
Why did they have to leave?

239
00:13:44,460 --> 00:13:45,420
I'm sorry.

240
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:46,697
Please forgive me.

241
00:13:46,780 --> 00:13:47,877
Rick, that's enough.

242
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:49,297
Leave him alone now, dear.

243
00:13:49,380 --> 00:13:50,937
You don't have to be so sad.

244
00:13:51,020 --> 00:13:54,549
They'll come back after they've
become fine marine officers.

245
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:02,380
What good is this?

246
00:14:02,560 --> 00:14:05,517
How are we supposed to become
marines by mopping floors?

247
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:09,017
Did you ever think that maybe this
is just a hobby that old geezer has?

248
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:09,930
A hobby?

249
00:14:10,540 --> 00:14:11,370
Yeah,

250
00:14:11,453 --> 00:14:14,457
a new hobby called tormenting
poor chore boys just for fun I'm

251
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:16,977
telling you the old man's crazy
enough that it might be true.

252
00:14:17,060 --> 00:14:18,097
Think about it for a sec.

253
00:14:18,180 --> 00:14:19,827
Would you bird stop chiming?

254
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:42,020
I love you.
